      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright © 2015 SPLF. Published by Elsevier Masson SAS. All rights reserved.",
        "AbstractText": [
          {
            "NlmCategory": "BACKGROUND",
            "Label": "INTRODUCTION",
            "content": "The hyper-IgG4 syndrome is an emerging disease with various thoracic manifestations: eosinophilic asthma, adenomegalies or mediastinal fibrosis, asthma, infiltrative pneumonia, nodules or pseudo-tumors with bronchial and pleural localizations."
          },
          {
            "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
            "Label": "CASE REPORT",
            "content": "We report the case of a 38-year-old woman who was admitted for acute exacerbation of eosinophilic asthma with high total IgE levels. A medical history of idiopathic acute pancreatitis, associated with sclerosing cholangitis and renal failure, suggested a diagnosis of hyper-IgG4 syndrome in this woman with late-onset severe and non-atopic asthma. A previous hepatic histology and a reinterpretation of renal tomodensitometry have confirmed this hypothesis."
          },
          {
            "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
            "Label": "CONCLUSION",
            "content": "The hyper-IgG4 syndrome is responsible of different clinico-radiological patterns that should be evoked because of the pejorative evolution of this steroid sensitive disease."
          }
        ]
      },
